   "newText": "Do not output the union or the holes.\n\n## ARC tiled-grid line fill (task-6b2b0ee9)\nWhen an input is partitioned by full-width/full-height color-8 separator lines into a regular array of square tiles, inspect the same local coordinates in each tile. Matching nonzero markers of one color that lie in a common tile-row or tile-column define a straight run across the tile array between their tile positions, inclusive. Fill every tile in that run uniformly with that marker color, replacing the whole tile interior (including the marker). Keep the separator lines color 8. When runs of different colors cross, use their digit sum at overlap (2+3 becomes 6). Leave tiles outside the marker-to-marker runs unchanged; a trailing partial tile beyond the complete tile array is not included in a run.\n\nEvidence: task-6b2b0ee9 demo had 22x22 grid with 8 dividers every 4 rows/columns and 3x3 tile interiors: two 2 markers at corresponding local positions in tile coordinates (row 0,col 1) and (row 4,col 1) produced color-2 fill in all five tile interiors of that vertical run; two 3 markers at (tile row 2, columns 0 and 4) produced a horizontal color-3 run; intersection tile became 6. The input test had 28x28 grid with dividers every 5 rows/columns and 4x4 tiles: the 2 pair in tile row 1, columns 0 and 4 filled that horizontal run, the 3 pair in tile column 2, tile rows 0 and 4 filled its vertical run, and intersection was 6. The incomplete final tile row/column remained unfilled. Preserve all 8 separator pixels exactly.\n"
